---
# Saved pages & app (/offline/ and /es/offline/): the one page for a weak signal — the pages saved on
# this device, how the site works without a connection, and the steps to install it as an app (they
# had a page of their own: app-redirect.njk keeps its address and #guide links working). The footer's
# bottom bar and the phone menu's "More" link here ("Saved pages & app", nav.js), and so do the Aa
# panel's "See saved pages" and install row, the offline notice and the install notice's "Show me
# how" (with the visitor's own guide as the #fragment). A real page: in the sitemap (REQUIRED there),
# the site's search (library.js walks nav.footer; search.page_desc.offline, search.kw.offline) and
# search engines (canonical + hreflang, base.njk). Send it to a group as …/offline/#steps: it opens
# each phone's guide.
# It is also the service worker's stand-in: src/pages/sw.11ty.js keeps both languages in its app shell
# and shows them — in the language of the address asked for — when a page is not saved on this device
# and there is no connection. The hero then says so from the first paint (the script after its
# buttons), and the list of saved pages follows — at the top of the page, whatever #fragment that
# address had. The list is read from the worker's caches by pwa.js (no JavaScript or no service
# worker: a plain note instead; forwarding pages — old addresses — are never listed).
pagination: { data: languages, size: 1, alias: lang }
permalink: "{{ '/' if lang == 'en' else '/es/' }}offline/index.html"
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: offline
titleKey: nav.offline
descKey: pwa.offline.meta_desc
---
{#- In this order: the hero · the pages saved on this device · how the site works without a connection
    (three cards: the pages you open are kept, "Save key pages" with its button, Data saver) · #steps,
    installing the site as an app: three notes (JavaScript only) and seven guides, one <details> per
    phone and browser, in this order — their ids are the #fragments the other pages use:
      iphone         iPhone or iPad, Safari (step 1 in four versions, [data-pwa-v] below)
      iphone-other   iPhone or iPad, Chrome / Edge / Firefox (from iOS 16.4)
      android        Android, Chrome ("Install", not "Create shortcut": shortcuts open in Chrome)
      samsung        Android, Samsung Internet
      android-other  Android, Firefox / Edge / Opera / Brave and others
      in-app         a page opened inside Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp … (those can't install): open
                     it in the phone's browser, or Copy the link
      computer       Chrome / Edge / Safari on a computer
    · "Why install it" (three cards) · "Good to know" (free, the Android shortcuts — the same three as
    the manifest's, src/pages/manifest.11ty.js —, removing it, the magazines' own apps).
    The contract with pwa.js (header items 5 and 6; install-core.js tells which device this is):
      [data-pwa-offline-copy]               the hero's buttons, with the hero's other words: standing
                                            in (data-title-standin, data-sub-standin — the script right
                                            after them — and data-hash, the #fragment it took off the
                                            address) and opened on purpose (data-sub-online, or
                                            data-sub-offline while there is no connection — pwa.js)
      [data-pwa-retry] (hidden)             "Try again": only while standing in for another page
      [data-pwa-steps-link] · [data-pwa-install-hero]   "How to install the app" (to the visitor's
                                            guide) or the one-tap "Install the app", one shown at a time;
                                            neither while standing in nor in the installed app
      [data-pwa-saved] …                    the list of saved pages (pwa.js offlineList)
      [data-pwa-save]                       the "Save key pages" button (pwa.js; empty without it)
      section[data-pwa-app]                 the guides — pwa.js only works where they are
      details#<id>[data-pwa-guide=<id>]     a guide: the visitor's opens, and so does any #<id> in the address
      [data-pwa-here] (hidden)              "Your device", in the summary of the visitor's guide
      [data-pwa-v=any|27|26|share]          Safari's step 1: "any" (it names each button) shows without
                                            JavaScript; the others are rendered hidden and pwa.js shows
                                            the one for this Safari — Page Menu (27), More (26), Share
      [data-pwa-inapp] (hidden)             "You're reading this inside {app}": data-t, {app} = the app's
                                            name or data-t-other, written into [data-pwa-inapp-text]
      [data-pwa-using] / [data-pwa-known]   "You're using the app" (in the app) / "already on this device"
      [data-pwa-not-in=<app>]               a tip hidden while reading inside that app's own browser
                                            (the WhatsApp tip inside WhatsApp: the note says it already)
      [data-pwa-act="install"]              one-tap install (the browser's own prompt)
      [data-copy] / [data-share]            app.js GV.copy / GV.share, with the address of the steps
    Printed, every guide is open (pwa.js). The words on the platforms' own buttons live in
    src/_i18n/pwa.json (pwa.app.* — tests/test_pwa_install.py pins them): re-check them every
    September (a new iOS) and after big Chrome releases, against the official help pages linked
    here (config/site.yml links: app_help_iphone, app_help_android, and their _es). -#}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{#- the address "Send this page" and "Copy the link" hand on: the steps, in this page's language -#}
{%- set appUrl = (page.url | siteUrl(site)) + "#steps" -%}
{%- set ln = site.links -%}
{%- set how = [
  { icon: "history", tone: "bg-gv-soft text-gv", h: "pwa.offline.how1_h", t: "pwa.offline.how1_t" },
  { icon: "hard-drive-download", tone: "bg-vine-soft text-vine", h: "pwa.offline.how2_h", t: "pwa.offline.how2_t", save: true },
  { icon: "gauge", tone: "bg-lv-soft text-lv", h: "pwa.offline.how3_h", t: "pwa.offline.how3_t" }
] -%}
{#- The button to look for, drawn in a small tile before a step's words: a Lucide icon (or the local
    safari-menu, Safari 27's Page Menu), or "app" = the app's own icon (open it from the home screen). -#}
{% macro key(name) -%}
<span class="pwa-guide-key" aria-hidden="true">{% if name == "app" %}<img src="/assets/img/app-icon-192.png" alt="" width="20" height="20">{% else %}{% icon name, "size-4" %}{% endif %}</span>
{%- endmacro %}
{#- A guide: steps (numbered; key + words k + an optional tip — or v, Safari's step-1 versions
    [variant, key, words, tip]) or list (the browsers of a group, not numbered); lead (a line before
    them), copy (Copy the link), tips (info lines: a key, or { k, notIn } — hidden inside that app),
    help ([link, label] of the official help page). -#}
{%- set guides = [
  { id: "iphone", icon: "smartphone", tone: "bg-gv-soft text-gv", h: "pwa.app.os_iphone", steps: [
      { v: [["any", "share", "pwa.app.ios_1", ""], ["27", "safari-menu", "pwa.app.ios_1_27", "pwa.app.ios_share_tip"],
            ["26", "circle-ellipsis", "pwa.app.ios_1_26", "pwa.app.ios_share_tip"], ["share", "share", "pwa.app.ios_1_share", ""]] },
      { key: "square-plus", k: "pwa.app.ios_2", tip: "pwa.app.ios_2_tip" },
      { key: "toggle-right", k: "pwa.app.ios_3" },
      { key: "app", k: "pwa.app.done" }
    ], tips: ["pwa.app.ios_fix", "pwa.app.ios_from_app"],
    help: [ln.app_help_iphone_es if lang == "es" else ln.app_help_iphone, "pwa.app.help_apple"] },
  { id: "iphone-other", icon: "smartphone", tone: "bg-gv-soft text-gv", h: "pwa.app.os_iphone_other", steps: [
      { key: "share", k: "pwa.app.ios_other_1" },
      { key: "square-plus", k: "pwa.app.ios_other_2" },
      { key: "app", k: "pwa.app.done" }
    ], tips: ["pwa.app.ios_other_old"] },
  { id: "android", icon: "smartphone", tone: "bg-vine-soft text-vine", h: "pwa.app.os_android", steps: [
      { key: "ellipsis-vertical", k: "pwa.app.android_1" },
      { key: "monitor-down", k: "pwa.app.android_2" },
      { key: "download", k: "pwa.app.android_3" },
      { key: "app", k: "pwa.app.done" }
    ], tips: ["pwa.app.android_fix", "pwa.app.android_from_app"],
    help: [ln.app_help_android_es if lang == "es" else ln.app_help_android, "pwa.app.help_google"] },
  { id: "samsung", icon: "smartphone", tone: "bg-grape-soft text-grape", h: "pwa.app.os_samsung", steps: [
      { key: "menu", k: "pwa.app.samsung_1" },
      { key: "square-plus", k: "pwa.app.samsung_2" },
      { key: "download", k: "pwa.app.samsung_3" },
      { key: "app", k: "pwa.app.done" }
    ], tips: ["pwa.app.samsung_tip"] },
  { id: "android-other", icon: "smartphone", tone: "bg-grape-soft text-grape", h: "pwa.app.os_android_other", list: [
      { key: "ellipsis-vertical", k: "pwa.app.other_firefox" },
      { key: "ellipsis", k: "pwa.app.other_edge" },
      { key: "menu", k: "pwa.app.other_rest" }
    ], tips: ["pwa.app.other_tip"] },
  { id: "in-app", icon: "external-link", tone: "bg-lv-soft text-lv", h: "pwa.app.os_in_app", lead: "pwa.app.inapp_t", steps: [
      { key: "ellipsis", k: "pwa.app.inapp_1" },
      { key: "external-link", k: "pwa.app.inapp_2" },
      { key: "list-ordered", k: "pwa.app.inapp_3" }
    ], copy: true, tips: [{ k: "pwa.app.inapp_whatsapp", notIn: "WhatsApp" }] },
  { id: "computer", icon: "monitor", tone: "bg-gv-soft text-gv", h: "pwa.app.os_computer", list: [
      { key: "monitor-down", k: "pwa.app.pc_chrome" },
      { key: "app-window", k: "pwa.app.pc_safari" },
      { key: "globe", k: "pwa.app.pc_other" }
    ] }
] -%}
{#- (working with a weak signal is the section "How the site works without a connection", above) -#}
{%- set why = [
  { icon: "smartphone", tone: "bg-gv-soft text-gv", h: "pwa.app.why1_h", t: "pwa.app.why1_t" },
  { icon: "languages", tone: "bg-grape-soft text-grape", h: "pwa.app.why2_h", t: "pwa.app.why2_t" },
  { icon: "refresh-cw", tone: "bg-lv-soft text-lv", h: "pwa.app.why3_h", t: "pwa.app.why3_t" }
] -%}
{#- the magazines' own apps (not this one): La Viña's first on the Spanish page -#}
{%- set magApps = [[ln.gv_apps, "media.short_gv_app", "en"], [ln.lv_apps, "media.short_lv_app", "es"]] -%}

{#- The hero's right-hand card (the shared hero aside, "Join by phone"): no data needed to reach a
    meeting — a one-tap call (the number, then the meeting ID) to the committee meeting and to the
    weekly open meetings (site.phone_access + the meeting IDs, eleventy/filters/access.js axPhone, the
    same as /accessibility/#phone, which it links to). The first card under the hero on smaller
    screens and at larger text ("below"): a phone with no signal is where it helps most. -#}
{%- set phone = site | axPhone(db.weekly_open.items | cmWeeklyAll(lang), lang) -%}
{% call(slot) ui.pageHero(lang, "nav.offline" | t(lang), "pwa.offline.sub_online" | t(lang), "", "pwa.offline.eyebrow" | t(lang), { eyebrowIcon: "wifi-off", titleId: "offline-title", side: "below" }) %}
{%- if slot == "side" %}
  {%- if phone.ok %}
  {% call ui.heroAside("pwa.offline.phone_title" | t(lang), lang, { id: "pwa-phone-title", icon: "phone", lead: "pwa.offline.phone_lead" | t(lang), href: ("/accessibility/" | lurl(lang)) + "#phone", linkLabel: "pwa.offline.phone_link" | t(lang) }) %}
  <ul class="hero-aside-links" role="list">
    {%- for mt in phone.meetings %}{% if mt.call and loop.index <= 3 %}
    {#- "Call now (Houston) · ID 871 2036 8287": the ID keeps a line of its own where it fits (an
        inline-block, "ID" and the number joined by a no-break space) and wraps only between its digit
        groups where it doesn't — never inside one (a narrow phone at 150 %) -#}
    {%- set callText = (("pwa.offline.phone_call" | t(lang, { city: mt.callCity })) | escape) ~ " · " ~ '<span class="inline-block">' ~ (("pwa.offline.phone_id" | t(lang, { id: mt.id })) | escape) ~ "</span>" %}
    <li>{{ ui.heroAsideLink({ href: mt.call, label: ("nav.meeting" if mt.key == "committee" else "access.aud_weekly_t") | t(lang), text: callText | safe, icon: "phone-call", tone: ("vine" if mt.key == "committee" else "grape") }, lang) }}</li>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endcall %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- else %}
{#- Opened on purpose: "How to install the app" (→ the visitor's guide) · "Install the app" (one tap —
    only while the browser offers it; then it takes the place of the other) · "Send this page" (share
    sheet, else Copy). The two install controls name the app themselves: the hero's title is the whole
    page's. Standing in for a page that isn't saved: "Try again" alone (it reloads that address). -#}
<div class="hero-actions" data-pwa-offline-copy
     data-title-standin="{{ 'pwa.offline.title' | t(lang) }}" data-sub-standin="{{ 'pwa.offline.sub' | t(lang) }}"
     data-sub-online="{{ 'pwa.offline.sub_online' | t(lang) }}" data-sub-offline="{{ 'pwa.offline.sub_direct' | t(lang) }}">
  <a class="btn-light" href="{{ '/' | lurl(lang) }}" data-pwa-retry hidden>{% icon "refresh-cw", "size-4" %} <span>{{ "pwa.offline.retry" | t(lang) }}</span></a>
  <a class="btn-light" href="#steps" data-pwa-steps-link>{% icon "list-ordered", "size-4" %} {{ "pwa.app.cta_steps" | t(lang) }}</a>
  <button type="button" class="btn-light" data-pwa-act="install" data-pwa-install-hero hidden>{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "pwa.app.cta_install" | t(lang) }}</button>
  <button type="button" class="btn-on-dark" data-js-only data-share="{{ appUrl }}" data-share-title="{{ 'pwa.app.title' | t(lang) }}" data-share-text="{{ 'pwa.app.send_text' | t(lang) }}">{% icon "share-2", "size-4" %} {{ "pwa.app.cta_send" | t(lang) }}</button>
</div>
{#- The hero's script, read with the page — before the first paint, and before the browser looks for
    the address's #fragment. (Here, inside the hero, right after what it changes: a script between the
    hero and the saved pages would keep the saved pages' card from spacing itself under the "Join by
    phone" card, main.css.)
    * Standing in for a page that isn't saved — the service worker's answer at that page's address, so
      JavaScript is on: the hero (and the tab's title) says "You're offline" and "This page isn't saved
      on this device yet…", and "Try again" (that address) is its one button. The address's #fragment
      belongs to the page asked for (/gvr/#steps), yet this page has ids of its own (#steps, the
      guides) the browser would jump to, past the hero and the saved pages: it comes off the address,
      kept in data-hash, and pwa.js puts it back before reloading. pwa.js tells standing in the same
      way (isFallback) and reloads the page once the connection is back.
    * Opened on purpose again — a reload, Back: the browser puts the visitor back where they were, but
      Chrome first jumps to a #guide in the address when it can't do that at once (the saved pages,
      listed a moment later, make the page taller than its first layout). The #fragment comes off for
      the load and back on once it is done; meanwhile data-hash-load keeps it, so pwa.js still opens
      that guide (a shared /offline/#iphone reloaded on an Android phone stays open). -#}
<script>(function (box) {
  try {
    if (!box) return;
    if (location.pathname.replace(/index\.html$/, "") === {{ (page.url | url) | dump | safe }}) {
      var nav = performance.getEntriesByType ? performance.getEntriesByType("navigation")[0] : null, h = location.hash;
      if (h && nav && (nav.type === "reload" || nav.type === "back_forward")) {
        // (data-hash-load: pwa.js still opens that guide while the #fragment is off the address)
        box.setAttribute("data-hash-load", h);
        history.replaceState(history.state, "", location.pathname + location.search);
        addEventListener("load", function () { history.replaceState(history.state, "", location.pathname + location.search + h); box.removeAttribute("data-hash-load"); });
      }
      return;
    }
    var hero = box.closest("[data-gv-hero]"), title = box.getAttribute("data-title-standin"), rest = document.title.indexOf(" · ");
    hero.querySelector(".gv-hero-title > span:last-child").textContent = title;
    hero.querySelector(".gv-hero-sub").textContent = box.getAttribute("data-sub-standin");
    document.title = title + (rest < 0 ? "" : document.title.slice(rest));
    for (var i = 0; i < box.children.length; i++) box.children[i].hidden = !box.children[i].hasAttribute("data-pwa-retry");
    box.querySelector("[data-pwa-retry]").setAttribute("href", location.pathname + location.search);
    if (location.hash) { box.setAttribute("data-hash", location.hash); history.replaceState(history.state, "", location.pathname + location.search); }
  } catch (e) { /* the page's own words stay */ }
})(document.querySelector("[data-pwa-offline-copy]"));</script>
{%- endif %}
{% endcall %}

{#- ============ The pages saved on this device (read from the service worker's caches) ============ -#}
<section class="container-page page-overlap" aria-labelledby="pwa-saved-h">
  <div class="card card-pad" data-pwa-saved
       data-t-saved="{{ 'pwa.offline.group_saved' | t(lang) }}" data-t-recent="{{ 'pwa.offline.group_recent' | t(lang) }}">
    <h2 id="pwa-saved-h" class="card-h"><span>{% icon "hard-drive-download", "size-5" %}</span><span>{{ "pwa.offline.list_h" | t(lang) }}</span></h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted" data-js-only data-pwa-saved-status role="status">{{ "pwa.offline.loading" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <noscript><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{{ "pwa.offline.nojs" | t(lang) }}</p></noscript>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted" data-pwa-saved-unsupported hidden>{{ "pwa.offline.unsupported" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <div class="mt-5" data-pwa-saved-empty hidden>{{ ui.emptyState("hard-drive", "pwa.offline.empty_title" | t(lang), "pwa.offline.empty_text" | t(lang)) }}</div>
    <div class="pwa-saved-groups" data-pwa-saved-list></div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============ How it works (what a visitor can do about a weak signal; installing is #steps) ============ -#}
<section class="section container-page pt-10 sm:pt-12" aria-labelledby="pwa-how-h">
  {{ ui.sectionHead("pwa.offline.how_h" | t(lang), "pwa.offline.how_sub" | t(lang), "", "", "wifi", { eyebrow: "pwa.offline.how_eyebrow" | t(lang), tone: "text-vine", id: "pwa-how-h", lang: lang }) }}
  <ul class="grid-cards-4" role="list">
    {% for c in how %}
    <li class="card card-pad flex flex-col gap-3">
      <span class="grid size-11 place-items-center rounded-xl {{ c.tone }}">{% icon c.icon, "size-5" %}</span>
      <h3 class="h-card">{{ c.h | t(lang) }}</h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ c.t | t(lang) }}</p>
      {#- pwa.js: the save button (disabled while offline; empty without JavaScript → hidden) -#}
      {% if c.save %}<div class="pwa-card-slot mt-auto empty:hidden" data-pwa-save></div>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

{#- ============ Install the app: one guide per phone and browser (the visitor's opened by pwa.js) ============ -#}
<section id="steps" class="section container-page pt-0" aria-labelledby="app-steps-h" data-pwa-app>
  {{ ui.sectionHead("pwa.app.title" | t(lang), "pwa.app.steps_sub" | t(lang), "", "", "list-ordered", { eyebrow: "pwa.app.steps_eyebrow" | t(lang), id: "app-steps-h", lang: lang }) }}
  {#- pwa.js shows the one that applies (none without JavaScript) -#}
  <div class="pwa-guide-notes">
    <div class="pwa-guide-note" data-pwa-inapp data-t="{{ 'pwa.app.inapp_now' | t(lang) }}" data-t-other="{{ 'pwa.app.inapp_other' | t(lang) }}" hidden>
      {% icon "external-link", "size-5" %}<p class="min-w-0" data-pwa-inapp-text></p>
    </div>
    <div class="pwa-guide-note is-ok" data-pwa-using hidden>
      {% icon "circle-check", "size-5" %}
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <p class="font-semibold">{{ "pwa.app.using_h" | t(lang) }}</p>
        <p>{{ "pwa.app.using_t" | t(lang) }} <a class="link" href="{{ '/' | lurl(lang) }}">{{ "pwa.offline.home" | t(lang) }}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pwa-guide-note is-ok" data-pwa-known hidden>
      {% icon "circle-check", "size-5" %}<p class="min-w-0">{{ "pwa.app.known" | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="pwa-guide">
    {%- for g in guides %}
    <details class="pwa-guide-os card" id="{{ g.id }}" data-pwa-guide="{{ g.id }}">
      <summary>
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl {{ g.tone }}">{% icon g.icon, "size-5" %}</span>
        {#- "Your device" flows after the title and wraps under it on a narrow phone -#}
        <span class="pwa-guide-title min-w-0 flex-1">{{ g.h | t(lang) }} <span class="badge-vine pwa-guide-here" data-pwa-here hidden>{{ "pwa.app.here" | t(lang) }}</span></span>
        <span class="pwa-guide-chev" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "chevron-down", "size-5" %}</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="pwa-guide-body">
        {%- if g.lead %}
        <p class="pwa-guide-lead">{{ g.lead | t(lang) }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if g.steps %}
        <ol class="pwa-guide-steps" role="list">
          {%- for s in g.steps %}{% set n = loop.index %}
          <li class="pwa-guide-step">
            <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ n }}</span>
            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
              {%- if s.v %}{% for x in s.v %}
              <div data-pwa-v="{{ x[0] }}"{% if x[0] != "any" %} hidden{% endif %}>
                <p><span class="sr-only">{{ n }}. </span>{{ key(x[1]) }}{{ x[2] | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
                {%- if x[3] %}
                <p class="pwa-guide-tip">{{ x[3] | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
                {%- endif %}
              </div>
              {%- endfor %}{% else %}
              <p><span class="sr-only">{{ n }}. </span>{{ key(s.key) }}{{ s.k | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
              {%- if s.tip %}
              <p class="pwa-guide-tip">{{ s.tip | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
              {%- endif %}{% endif %}
            </div>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if g.list %}
        <ul class="pwa-guide-steps" role="list">
          {%- for s in g.list %}
          <li class="pwa-guide-step"><p class="min-w-0">{{ key(s.key) }}{{ s.k | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</p></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if g.copy or g.tips or (g.help and g.help[0]) %}
        <div class="pwa-guide-more">
          {%- if g.copy %}
          {#- the address to paste into Safari or Chrome (JavaScript: a Copy button; without it: the address itself) -#}
          <p class="text-ink">{{ "pwa.app.inapp_copy" | t(lang) }}</p>
          <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
            <button type="button" class="btn-secondary btn-sm" data-js-only data-copy="{{ appUrl }}">{% icon "copy", "size-4" %} {{ "pwa.app.copy_link" | t(lang) }}</button>
            <span class="break-all font-medium text-ink" data-nojs-only>{{ appUrl }}</span>
          </p>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- for tip in g.tips %}
          <p class="pwa-guide-tip flex gap-2"{% if tip.notIn %} data-pwa-not-in="{{ tip.notIn }}"{% endif %}>{% icon "info", "size-4" %}<span class="min-w-0">{{ (tip.k or tip) | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</span></p>
          {%- endfor %}
          {%- if g.help and g.help[0] %}
          <p class="pwa-guide-tip">{{ "pwa.app.help" | t(lang) }} <a class="link" href="{{ g.help[0] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ g.help[1] | t(lang) }}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a></p>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </details>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{#- ============ Why install it ============ -#}
<section class="section container-page pt-0" aria-labelledby="app-why-h">
  {{ ui.sectionHead("pwa.app.why_h" | t(lang), "", "", "", "sparkles", { eyebrow: "pwa.app.why_eyebrow" | t(lang), tone: "text-grape", id: "app-why-h", lang: lang }) }}
  <ul class="grid-cards-4" role="list">
    {%- for c in why %}
    <li class="card card-pad flex flex-col gap-3">
      <span class="grid size-11 place-items-center rounded-xl {{ c.tone }}">{% icon c.icon, "size-5" %}</span>
      <h3 class="h-card">{{ c.h | t(lang) }}</h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ c.t | t(lang) }}</p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

{#- ============ Good to know ============ -#}
<section class="section container-page pt-0" aria-labelledby="app-more-h">
  <div class="panel-muted">
    <h2 id="app-more-h" class="card-h"><span>{% icon "info", "size-5" %}</span>{{ "pwa.app.more_h" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed lg:grid-cols-2" role="list">
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-gv">{% icon "shield-check", "size-4" %}</span><span class="min-w-0 text-ink">{{ "pwa.app.more_free" | t(lang) }}</span></li>
      {#- the manifest's three shortcuts (src/pages/manifest.11ty.js), by their menu names -#}
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-gv">{% icon "hand", "size-4" %}</span><span class="min-w-0 text-ink">{{ "pwa.app.more_shortcuts" | t(lang, { a: "nav.meetings" | t(lang), b: "nav.monthly" | t(lang), c: "nav.orientation" | t(lang) }) }}</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-gv">{% icon "trash-2", "size-4" %}</span><span class="min-w-0 text-ink">{{ "pwa.app.more_remove" | t(lang) | mdInline | safe }}</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-gv">{% icon "grapes", "size-4" %}</span><span class="min-w-0 text-ink">{{ "pwa.app.more_magazines" | t(lang) }}{% for m in (magApps | reverse if lang == "es" else magApps) %}{% if m[0] %}{{ " " }}{% if not loop.first %}<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>{{ " " }}{% endif %}<a class="link" href="{{ m[0] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% if m[2] != lang %} hreflang="{{ m[2] }}"{% endif %}>{{ m[1] | t(lang) }}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
